d="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" class="markdown-body" data-turbolinks="false"><div class="markdown-body NewMarkdownViewer-module__safe-html-box__ZT1eD"><p dir="auto">The main idea is to offer mapping from a list into a map and vice versa. This could be done by treating the map as an <code class="notranslate">Iterable&lt;Map.Entry&lt;K,V&gt;&gt;</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This would me that we could do something like:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-java notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="// First example
--
    @Mapping(target = &quot;day&quot;, source = &quot;key&quot;)
    @Mapping(target = &quot;.&quot;, source = &quot;value&quot;)
    FlattenedTarget map(Map.Entry&lt;String, Source&gt; entry);
}

--
    @Mapping(target = &quot;day&quot;, source = &quot;key&quot;)
    @Mapping(target = &quot;times&quot;, source = &quot;value&quot;)
    FlattenedTarget map(Map.Entry&lt;String, Source&gt; entry);
}"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-c">// First example</span>
<span class="pl-c1">@</span><span class="pl-c1">Mapper</span>
--
    @Mapping(target = &quot;key&quot;, source = &quot;day&quot;)
    @Mapping(target = &quot;value&quot;, source = &quot;item&quot;)
    Map.Entry&lt;String, Target&gt; map(FlattenedSource item);

    Target map(FlattenedSource item);
--
    @Mapping(target = &quot;key&quot;, source = &quot;day&quot;)
    @Mapping(target = &quot;value&quot;, source = &quot;times&quot;)
    Map.Entry&lt;String, List&lt;String&gt; map(FlattenedSource item);
}"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-c">// First example</span>
<span class="pl-c1">@</span><span class="pl-c1">Mapper</span>
--
    <span class="pl-smi">Map</span>.<span class="pl-smi">Entry</span>&lt;<span class="pl-smi">String</span>, <span class="pl-smi">List</span>&lt;<span class="pl-smi">String</span>&gt; <span class="pl-en">map</span>(<span class="pl-smi">FlattenedSource</span> <span class="pl-s1">item</span>);
}</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">To support something like this we would have to provide a custom support for mapping to <code class="notranslate">Map.Entry</code> and to treat <code class="notranslate">Map&lt;K,V&gt;</code> as <code class="notranslate">Iterable&lt;Map.Entry&lt;K,V&gt;&gt;</code> when mapping a map into an iterable.</p>
